  "title": "April 2025 Anomalies",
  "turns": [
    {
      "jobId": "3607b827-f702-43c5-8e8b-6ba1e3e5776c",
      "question": "Using January 2 through March 31, 2025 as the baseline, which 10 sessions in April 2025 were the most unusual among the 50 most liquid US stocks, and which features made each one unusual? Anomaly scores are neither forecasts nor explanations.",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-01T18:55:10.634198Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-10-01T18:55:23.551406Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "All ten most unusual sessions in April 2025 among the top 50 most liquid US stocks occurred on **April 9, 2025**. The anomaly model (PCA reconstruction) compared each session against a January 2 – March 31, 2025 baseline using four features: 1-day return, 5-day return, 20-day realized volatility, and 20-day log-volume deviation. The “observed deviations” below are robust z-scores against that baseline (not returns or percentages); higher absolute values mean the feature contributed more to the anomaly score.\n\n| Rank | Asset | Date | Anomaly score | 1-day return (z) | 5-day return (z) | 20-day vol (z) | 20-day log-volume (z) |\n|------|-------|------|---------------|------------------|------------------|----------------|-----------------------|\n| 1 | AMD | 2025-04-09 | 11.54 | +12.75 | −1.22 | +5.72 | +2.55 |\n| 2 | MU | 2025-04-09 | 10.27 | +10.47 | −2.53 | +6.34 | +1.87 |\n| 3 | TSLA | 2025-04-09 | 10.16 | +12.32 | −0.76 | +6.47 | +2.02 |\n| 4 | AAPL | 2025-04-09 | 6.71 | +8.19 | −2.40 | +3.33 | +2.29 |\n| 5 | APP | 2025-04-09 | 6.38 | +9.07 | −1.13 | +8.34 | +0.92 |\n| 6 | INTC | 2025-04-09 | 5.42 | +9.24 | −0.32 | +5.44 | +1.48 |\n| 7 | TXN | 2025-04-09 | 5.31 | +8.49 | −1.03 | +3.37 | +2.34 |\n| 8 | COIN | 2025-04-09 | 5.06 | +8.42 | −0.86 | +4.39 | +2.25 |\n| 9 | QCOM | 2025-04-09 | 4.81 | +7.32 | −1.69 | +3.17 | +2.18 |\n| 10 | BA | 2025-04-09 | 4.77 | +7.97 | −0.96 | +3.78 | +1.16 |\n\n[1]\n\n**Limitations**: Anomaly scores describe unusual observed feature combinations; they are not forecasts or probabilities. Observed deviations are robust z-scores against the training window, not returns or percentages; they are descriptive reason codes and do not establish a cause or adverse event.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [1] Market analytics result — market anomaly scan — evidence `hermes-receipt:bdb74b2c384ef2bf939ae2a0e6338fc5ba81f8cc02442124114da68f18f118ec`",
